ity_name":"The Grand Opera House","title":"Catch a Community Production","subtitle":"West 8th Street at Iowa Street","notes":"Check the production calendar before walking down West 8th Street; the historic venue presents community-focused theatre, dance, and performing-arts programs.","short_summary":"A nineteenth-century theater still operating as a nonprofit performance venue.","evidence_claim":"The Grand Opera House documents that it has served Dubuque since 1890 and now operates as the city’s largest nonprofit theatre.","source_url":"https://thegrandoperahouse.com/","source_title":"The Grand Opera House","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Grand+Opera+House+135+W+8th+St+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"Entry generally depends on a scheduled performance or program; consult the official calendar and ticket details.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-washington-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Washington Park","title":"Pause at the Gazebo","subtitle":"Locust Street between West 6th and West 7th streets","notes":"Walk in from Locust Street and use the gazebo as your visual landmark; benches, picnic tables, vegetation, and a city time capsule fill the block.","short_summary":"A full downtown park block centered on a highly photographable gazebo.","evidence_claim":"The city locates Washington Park at 700 Locust Street and lists its gazebo, planted areas, time capsule, benches, picnic tables, and water fountains.","source_url":"https://cityofdubuque.org/2790/Washington-Park","source_title":"Washington Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Washington+Park+700+Locust+Street+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"The city lists seasonal park hours from 7 a.m. to 10 p.m.; amenities may be unavailable outside the stated park season.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-town-clock","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Dubuque Town Clock","title":"Frame the Clock from Main Street","subtitle":"Main Street at Town Clock Plaza","notes":"Stand back along Main Street to fit the elevated clock and its four-column pedestal into one frame, then compare the structure with nearby storefront scale.","short_summary":"A 110-foot downtown landmark raised above its pedestrian plaza.","evidence_claim":"The city says the Town Clock stands in Town Clock Plaza on Main Street, was moved there in 1971, and reaches approximately 110 feet when assembled.","source_url":"https://www.cityofdubuque.org/1596/Town-Clock","source_title":"Town Clock","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dubuque+Town+Clock+700+Main+Street+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"View the exterior from Town Clock Plaza; nearby festivals or street activity can temporarily affect access.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-five-flags-center","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Five Flags Center","title":"Use the Locust Street Entrance","subtitle":"Main Street between West 4th and West 5th streets","notes":"When attending an event, approach the Main Street venue from its signed Locust Street entrance between Fourth and Fifth streets and review the bag policy first.","short_summary":"A downtown civic and entertainment complex spanning an arena and historic theater.","evidence_claim":"Five Flags Center lists its address as 405 Main Street and specifies that its visitor entrance is on Locust Street between Fourth and Fifth streets.","source_url":"https://www.fiveflagscenter.com/directions.aspx","source_title":"Location & Directions","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Five+Flags+Center+405+Main+Street+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"Building entry is event-dependent; check the official schedule, ticket requirements, entrance details, and current bag policy.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-fenelon-place-elevator","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Fenelon Place Elevator","title":"Ride Above Fourth Street","subtitle":"West 4th Street at Bluff Street","notes":"Start at Fourth and Bluff for the lower station, bring cash for the fare, and ride the 296-foot funicular toward Fenelon Place for the elevated view.","short_summary":"A compact seasonal funicular climbing directly from downtown to the bluff.","evidence_claim":"The operator describes the Fenelon Place Elevator as a 296-foot funicular rising 189 feet from Fourth Street to Fenelon Place and directs GPS users to Fourth and Bluff streets.","source_url":"https://www.fenelonplaceelevator.com/","source_title":"Fenelon Place Elevator Company","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fenelon+Place+Elevator+4th+and+Bluff+Streets+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"The operator lists seasonal daily service from April 1 through November 30, excluding Thanksgiving, and says payment is cash only.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-river-museum","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"National Mississippi River Museum & Aquarium","title":"Follow Third Street to the River","subtitle":"East 3rd Street in the Port of Dubuque","notes":"Take the Third Street bridge toward the Port and follow the museum’s alternate directions if rail traffic blocks the more common Fifth Street approach.","short_summary":"A combined aquarium, river-history museum, and science center on the waterfront.","evidence_claim":"The museum locates its campus at 350 East 3rd Street in the Port of Dubuque and describes it as part museum, part aquarium, and part science center.","source_url":"https://www.rivermuseum.org/map","source_title":"Maps & Directions | National Mississippi River Museum & Aquarium","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=National+Mississippi+River+Museum+350+East+3rd+Street+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"Admission is ticketed; verify current hours and use the museum’s alternate route when train traffic obstructs the Fifth Street crossing.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"loras-shot-tower","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Dubuque Shot Tower","title":"Study the Stone-to-Brick Tower","subtitle":"Commercial Street at the Mississippi River","notes":"Approach from Commercial Street and study the exterior transition from seven stone stories to three brick stories; do not attempt to enter the structure.","short_summary":"A 120-foot industrial landmark built for nineteenth-century lead-shot production.","evidence_claim":"The city locates the Shot Tower at Commercial Street and the Mississippi River and documents its seven stone stories, three brick stories, and 120-foot height.","source_url":"https://www.cityofdubuque.org/712/Shot-Tower","source_title":"Shot Tower","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dubuque+Shot+Tower+Commercial+Street+Dubuque+IA","access_notes":"Treat this as an exterior landmark stop; the city page does not advertise public interior access.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
